wlanpi-core (2.1.19-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Add internal localhost/HMAC-only PAM endpoint (POST /api/v1/auth/pam) that
    verifies a local account password on behalf of wlanpi-webui, which runs
    unprivileged and cannot use pam_unix itself. The wlanpi-webui PAM service
    limits WebUI management access to the sudo group. No password is stored or
    logged; no Core token is issued.
  * Stop logging nginx request bodies (credentials could pass through the
    reverse proxy during login).
  * Add python-pam dependency and libpam0g/libpam-modules/libpam-runtime
    package dependencies.

 -- Josh Schmelzle <josh@joshschmelzle.com>  Thu, 17 Sep 2026 16:20:00 -0400

wlanpi-core (2.1.18-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Self-signed TLS certs cover the renamed .local hostname
    (wlanpi-<mac-suffix>.local) and regenerate when an existing cert predates
    it (fixes hostname mismatch warnings for nginx, WebUI, Grafana, Cockpit).
    Cert generation is extracted into a shared script used by postinst and the
    first-boot UFW setup. (#175)

