wlanpi-core (2.1.12-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fail the ASGI lifespan on critical init failure (system readiness,
    security, database) so systemd's restart policy engages instead of
    serving half-initialized; token-manager failure stays non-fatal
  * Fix undefined initial_retry_delay AttributeError in the security-init
    retry path
  * systemd: remove duplicate Type=notify; add bounded Restart=on-failure
    policy (RestartSec=2, StartLimitIntervalSec=60, StartLimitBurst=5),
    TimeoutStartSec=30, RequiresMountsFor, ExecStartPre writability probe
  * Bind absolute /run/wlanpi_core.sock matching the socket unit and nginx
    proxy_pass (was relative, resolving to a different socket)
  * prerm: fix mount-unit name (var-log-wlanpi_core-debug.mount); add
    #DEBHELPER# so the service and socket are stopped on removal

